#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:1
msgid "Release 2.29.0 (2025-05-14)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:3
msgid ""
"After the special backport-based release of Nix 2.28 (timed to coincide with "
"Nixpkgs 25.05), the release process is back to normal with 2.29. As such, we "
"have slightly more weeks of work from `master` (since 2.28 was branched from "
"2.27) than usual. This fact is counterbalanced by the fact that most of "
"those changes are bug fixes rather than larger new features."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:7
msgid ""
"Prettified JSON output on the terminal [\\#12555](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/issues/12555) [\\#12652](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/12652)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:9
msgid "This makes the output easier to read."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:11
msgid ""
"Scripts are mostly unaffected because for those, stdout will be a file or a "
"pipe, not a terminal, and for those, the old single-line behavior applies."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:13
msgid ""
"`--json --pretty` can be passed to enable it even if the output is not a "
"terminal. If your script creates a pseudoterminal for Nix's stdout, you can "
"pass `--no-pretty` to disable the new behavior."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:16
msgid ""
"Repl: improve continuation prompt for incomplete expressions [\\#12846]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/12846)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:18
msgid ""
"Improved REPL user experience by updating the continuation prompt from "
"invisible blank spaces to a visible `\" > \"`, enhancing clarity when "
"entering multi-line expressions."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:20
msgid ""
"REPL `:load-flake` and `:reload` now work together [\\#8753](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/issues/8753) [\\#13180](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/13180)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:22
msgid ""
"Previously, `:reload` only reloaded the files specified with `:load` (or on "
"the command line). Now, it also works with the flakes specified with `:load-"
"flake` (or on the command line). This makes it correctly reload everything "
"that was previously loaded, regardless of what sort of thing (plain file or "
"flake) each item is."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:26
msgid ""
"Increase retry delays on HTTP 429 Too Many Requests [\\#13052](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13052)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:28
msgid ""
"When downloading Nix, the retry delay was previously set to 0.25 seconds. It "
"has now been increased to 1 minute to better handle transient CI errors, "
"particularly on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:30
msgid ""
"S3: opt-in the STSProfileCredentialsProvider [\\#12646](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/12646)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:32
msgid ""
"Added support for STS-based authentication for S3-based binary caches, i.e. "
"enabling seamless integration with `aws sso login`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:34
msgid ""
"Reduce connect timeout for http substituter [\\#12876](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/12876)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:36
msgid ""
"Previously, the Nix setting `connect-timeout` had no limit. It is now set to "
"`5s`, offering a more practical default for users self-hosting binary "
"caches, which may occasionally become unavailable, such as during updates."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:39
msgid ""
"C API: functions for locking and loading a flake [\\#10435](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/issues/10435) [\\#12877](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/12877) [\\#13098](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13098)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:41
msgid ""
"This release adds functions to the C API for handling the loading of flakes. "
"Previously, this had to be worked around by using `builtins.getFlake`. C API "
"consumers and language bindings now have access to basic locking "
"functionality."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:44
msgid ""
"It does not expose the full locking API, so that the implementation can "
"evolve more freely. Locking is controlled with the functions, which cover "
"the common use cases for consuming a flake:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:46
msgid "`nix_flake_lock_flags_set_mode_check`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:47
msgid "`nix_flake_lock_flags_set_mode_virtual`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:48
msgid "`nix_flake_lock_flags_set_mode_write_as_needed`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:49
msgid "`nix_flake_lock_flags_add_input_override`, which also enables `virtual`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:51
msgid ""
"This change also introduces the new `nix-fetchers-c` library, whose single "
"purpose for now is to manage the (`nix.conf`) settings for the built-in "
"fetchers."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:53
msgid "More details can be found in the [C API documentation](../c-api.md)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:55
msgid ""
"No longer copy flakes that are in the nix store [\\#10435](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/issues/10435) [\\#12877](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/12877) [\\#13098](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13098)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:57
msgid ""
"Previously, we would duplicate entries like `path:/nix/store/*` back into "
"the Nix store. This was prominently visible for pinned system flake registry "
"entries in NixOS, e.g., when running `nix run nixpkgs#hello`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:60
msgid ""
"Consistently preserve error messages from cached evaluation [\\#12762]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/12762) [\\#12809](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/12809)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:62
msgid ""
"In one code path, we are not returning the errors cached from prior "
"evaluation, but instead throwing generic errors stemming from the lack of "
"value (due to the error). These generic error messages were far less "
"informative. Now we consistently return the original error message."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:66
msgid ""
"Faster blake3 hashing [\\#12676](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/12676)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:68
msgid ""
"The implementation for blake3 hashing is now multi-threaded and used memory-"
"mapped IO. Benchmark results can be found the [pull request](https://github."
"com/NixOS/nix/pull/12676)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:71
msgid ""
"Fix progress bar for S3 binary caches and make file transfers interruptible "
"[\\#12877](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/12877) [\\#13098](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/13098) [\\#12538](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/12538)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:73
msgid ""
"The progress bar now correctly display upload/download progress for S3 up/"
"downloads. S3 uploads are now interruptible."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:75
msgid ""
"Add host attribute of github/gitlab flakerefs to URL serialization [\\#12580]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/12580)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:77
msgid ""
"Resolved an issue where `github:` or `gitlab:` URLs lost their `host` "
"attribute when written to a lockfile, resulting in invalid URLs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:79
msgid ""
"Multiple signatures support in store urls [\\#12976](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/12976)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:81
msgid ""
"Added support for a `secretKeyFiles` URI parameter in Nix store URIs, "
"allowing multiple signing key files to be specified as a comma-separated "
"list. This enables signing paths with multiple keys. This helps with [RFC "
"#149](https://github.com/NixOS/rfcs/pull/149) to enable binary cache key "
"rotation in the NixOS infra."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:84
msgid "Example usage:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:87
msgid "\"file:///tmp/store?secret-keys=/tmp/key1,/tmp/key2\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:88
msgid "\"$(nix build --print-out-paths nixpkgs#hello)\""
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:91
msgid ""
"nix flake show now skips over import-from-derivation [\\#4265](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/4265) [\\#12583](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/12583)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:93
msgid ""
"Previously, if a flake contained outputs relying on [import from derivation]"
"(../language/import-from-derivation.md) during evaluation, `nix flake show` "
"would fail to display the rest of the flake. The updated behavior skips such "
"outputs, allowing the rest of the flake to be shown."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:95
msgid ""
"Add `nix formatter build` and `nix formatter run` commands [\\#13063]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13063)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:97
msgid "`nix formatter run` is an alias for `nix fmt`. Nothing new there."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:99
msgid ""
"`nix formatter build` is sort of like `nix build`: it builds, links, and "
"prints a path to the formatter program:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:106
msgid ""
"Note that unlike `nix build`, this prints the full path to the program, not "
"just the store path (in the example above that would be `/nix/store/"
"cb9w44vkhk2x4adfxwgdkkf5gjmm856j-treefmt`)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:108
msgid ""
"Amend OSC 8 escape stripping for xterm-style separator [\\#13109](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13109)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.29.md:110
msgid ""
"Improve terminal escape code filtering to understand a second type of "
"hyperlink escape codes. This in particular prevents parts of GCC 14's "
"diagnostics from being improperly filtered away."
msgstr ""

